<title>SWEDEN: Foreningsbanken says '96 profit up 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Foreningsbanken says '96 profit up 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earnings for Swedish bank Foreningsbanken in 1996, released on Tuesday.</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit			 1,160  vs 1,020</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	    1.25  vs 0.50</p>
<p> Loan losses				1,091  vs 1,447</p>
<p> Net interest income		    3,613  vs 3,656</p>
<p> Commission				   840  vs 741</p>
<p> Interest receivable		   10,784  vs 11,770</p>
<p> Total income			     5,205  vs 5,398</p>
<p> Interest payable			 7,193  vs 8,139</p>
<p> Total costs				2,954  vs 2,931</p>
<p> Profit before loan losses	    2,251  vs 2,467</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,022  vs 1,017</p>
<p> Capital adequacy ratio (pct)	 13.6   vs 12.5</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	  3.92   vs 3.90</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuter poll showed analysts expected a profit, on average, of 1.13 billion crowns.  -- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
